1
00:00:01,370 --> 00:00:08,600
You read a reference passage describing river scene.

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:16,600
This canal is called Sun Canal.

3
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:26,330
Here all day long, sunshine pours down on earth.

4
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:34,460
Morning the canal is still peach color,

5
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:49,240
noon suddenly turns into a line of flowing mercury, dazzling,

6
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:59,370
then gradually turns into a fire stream at sunset.

7
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:10,420
Maybe that's why it's called Sun Canal.

8
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:18,150
Passage is described in which order?

9
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:26,480
A. Describe each feature of scene in turn.

10
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:34,100
B. Describe according to time order.

11
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:43,600
Answer B. Describe according to time order.

12
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:55,880
How is canal described at each time of day?

13
00:01:56,820 --> 00:02:06,710
Connect suitable descriptive phrase with each time.

14
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:18,110
Morning pink like peach fruit.

15
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:32,730
Noon white like mercury.

16
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:45,150
Afternoon red like fire.

17
00:02:47,750 --> 00:03:00,680
In your opinion, why is canal called Sun Canal?

